{"name":"Butternut Pie","hex":"#d99e66","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"butternut","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A North American walnut tree, Juglans cinerea.","The wood or bark of this walnut tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/butternut"},{"term":"pie","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Piro."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of pastry that consists of an outer crust and a filling. (Savory pies are more popular in the UK and sweet pies are more popular in the US, so \"pie\" without qualification has different connotations in these dialects.)","Any of various other, non-pastry dishes that maintain the general concept of a shell with a filling."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pie"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pie","blocks":[{"text":"A pie is a baked dish which is usually made of a pastry dough casing that contains a filling of various sweet or savoury ingredients. Sweet pies may be filled with fruit, nuts, fruit preserves, brown sugar, sweetened vegetables, or with thicker fillings based on eggs and dairy. Savoury pies may be filled with meat, eggs and cheese, or a mixture of meat and vegetables."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Top_down_view_of_peach_pie_%28722379748%29.jpg/330px-Top_down_view_of_peach_pie_%28722379748%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pie","wikidata":"Q13360264"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Redressed_birds_-_Jan_Brueghel_I_%26_Peter_Paul_Rubens_-_Taste_%28Museo_del_Prado%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Redressed_birds_-_Jan_Brueghel_I_%26_Peter_Paul_Rubens_-_Taste_%28Museo_del_Prado%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Redressed_birds_-_Jan_Brueghe